BND-10: evaluate control rules between events, as legacy does

SWMMEngine::stepRouting() returned as soon as the current time was outside
every [EVENTS] period, before the pump target settings and control rules were
evaluated, so no rule acted between events (a rule due at 01:00 acted when
the next event started). Legacy evaluateControlRules() runs before the event
test on every step and only the flow routing is skipped. Move the event test
and its early return below the control-rule block; its content is unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply BND-10_swmm600.patch

